  "term": "cerebral lesion",
  "definition": "In this historical source, a cerebral lesion means brain damage, especially after injury to the skull or brain, that is linked with both bodily symptoms and episodes of mental disturbance. It is described as sometimes improving, but in more severe cases following a progressive course toward lasting impairment or degeneration.",
